[{"id":4049,"date":"2026-07-07T17:27:27","date_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:57:27","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/?p=4049"},"modified":"2026-07-07T17:27:27","modified_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:57:27","slug":"why-gi-labs-canada-certification-matters-more-than-marketing-claims","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/why-gi-labs-canada-certification-matters-more-than-marketing-claims\/","title":{"rendered":"Why GI Labs Canada Certification Matters More Than Marketing Claims"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Walk through the health food aisle today and you&#8217;ll find countless products claiming to be &#8220;healthy,&#8221; &#8220;diabetic-friendly,&#8221; or &#8220;better for blood sugar.&#8221; The challenge isn&#8217;t finding claims\u2014it&#8217;s knowing which ones are backed by credible science.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That&#8217;s where independent testing makes all the difference.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sugarlif\u00ae Low GI Diet Sugar has been <strong>certified as a Low Glycemic Index (Low GI) product by GI Labs, Canada<\/strong>, one of the world&#8217;s leading laboratories dedicated to Glycemic Index testing. This isn&#8217;t a claim made by the manufacturer\u2014it&#8217;s the result of evaluation by an internationally recognized laboratory.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why does this matter?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The Glycemic Index (GI) measures how quickly a carbohydrate-containing food raises blood sugar levels after consumption. Foods with a lower GI release glucose more gradually, resulting in a slower and steadier rise in blood sugar compared to high-GI foods.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is why the GI of a food has become an important consideration for people who want to make informed dietary choices\u2014not just those living with diabetes, but also individuals interested in sustained energy, weight management, and overall metabolic health.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Science Over Slogans<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Anyone can print &#8220;healthy&#8221; on a package.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Very few products can point to independent scientific validation from a globally respected Glycemic Index laboratory.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">GI Labs, Canada has earned an international reputation for testing foods using established Glycemic Index protocols. Certification from such a laboratory gives consumers greater confidence that a product&#8217;s Low GI status is based on scientific evaluation rather than marketing language.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">More Than Just Another Sugar<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">What makes Sugarlif particularly interesting is that it begins as regular cane sugar but is processed using a proprietary natural treatment designed to lower its Glycemic Index while preserving the qualities people expect from sugar\u2014its taste, texture, colour, and functionality in everyday cooking and beverages. The product has been independently evaluated for its Low GI characteristics by leading international laboratories, including GI Labs in Canada.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Trust Built on Evidence<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In today&#8217;s world, consumers are becoming more informed than ever. They don&#8217;t simply ask, &#8220;Is this healthy?&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They ask:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Who tested it?<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Was it independently verified?<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Is there credible scientific evidence behind the claim?<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">These are exactly the questions that international laboratory certification helps answer.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When a product carries Low GI certification from GI Labs Canada, it represents a commitment to transparency, scientific evaluation, and consumer trust.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Because when it comes to health, confidence should come from evidence\u2014not advertising.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Walk through the health food aisle today and you&#8217;ll find countless products claiming to be &#8220;healthy,&#8221; &#8220;diabetic-friendly,&#8221; or &#8220;better for blood sugar.&#8221; The challenge isn&#8217;t finding claims\u2014it&#8217;s knowing which ones are backed by credible science. That&#8217;s where independent testing makes all the difference. Sugarlif\u00ae Low GI Diet Sugar has been certified as a Low Glycemic [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"site-sidebar-layout":"default","site-content-layout":"","ast-site-content-layout":"default","site-content-style":"default","site-sidebar-style":"default","ast-global-header-display":"","ast-banner-title-visibility":"","ast-main-header-display":"","ast-hfb-above-header-display":"","ast-hfb-below-header-display":"","ast-hfb-mobile-header-display":"","site-post-title":"","ast-breadcrumbs-content":"","ast-featured-img":"","footer-sml-layout":"","ast-disable-related-posts":"","theme-transparent-header-meta":"","adv-header-id-meta":"","stick-header-meta":"","header-above-stick-meta":"","header-main-stick-meta":"","header-below-stick-meta":"","astra-migrate-meta-layouts":"set","ast-page-background-enabled":"default","ast-page-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-4)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"ast-content-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4049","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-blog"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4049","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=4049"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4049\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4050,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4049\/revisions\/4050"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4049"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=4049"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=4049"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":4041,"date":"2026-07-07T17:03:40","date_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:33:40","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/?p=4041"},"modified":"2026-07-07T17:07:32","modified_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:37:32","slug":"episode-5-sugar-on-trial","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/episode-5-sugar-on-trial\/","title":{"rendered":"Sugar on Trial"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Court is now in session.<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The accused?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sugar.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The charges?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Being responsible for everything from afternoon naps to expanding waistlines.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The courtroom is packed.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Diet trends have arrived.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fitness influencers are taking notes.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Someone in the back is whispering about keto.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The judge enters.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;Order!&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The prosecution begins dramatically.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;Your Honour&#8230; sugar is guilty.&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The judge raises an eyebrow.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;Do you have evidence?&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Silence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Because science doesn&#8217;t convict based on rumours.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It asks better questions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Which sugar?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">How much?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Under what conditions?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">How was it tested?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That&#8217;s why independent laboratories matter.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They&#8217;re the expert witnesses.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They don&#8217;t shout.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They don&#8217;t speculate.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They simply present the evidence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For products like Sugarlif, that evidence includes internationally recognised Low GI testing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Not because science enjoys making life complicated.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Because health deserves something stronger than opinion.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The verdict?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Don&#8217;t believe everything you hear in the courtroom of public opinion.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sometimes the most important witness is the one wearing a lab coat.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Case closed.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Court is now in session. The accused? Sugar. The charges? Being responsible for everything from afternoon naps to expanding waistlines. The courtroom is packed. Diet trends have arrived. Fitness influencers are taking notes. Someone in the back is whispering about keto. The judge enters. &#8220;Order!&#8221; The prosecution begins dramatically. &#8220;Your Honour&#8230; sugar is guilty.&#8221; The [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"site-sidebar-layout":"default","site-content-layout":"","ast-site-content-layout":"default","site-content-style":"default","site-sidebar-style":"default","ast-global-header-display":"","ast-banner-title-visibility":"","ast-main-header-display":"","ast-hfb-above-header-display":"","ast-hfb-below-header-display":"","ast-hfb-mobile-header-display":"","site-post-title":"","ast-breadcrumbs-content":"","ast-featured-img":"","footer-sml-layout":"","ast-disable-related-posts":"","theme-transparent-header-meta":"","adv-header-id-meta":"","stick-header-meta":"","header-above-stick-meta":"","header-main-stick-meta":"","header-below-stick-meta":"","astra-migrate-meta-layouts":"set","ast-page-background-enabled":"default","ast-page-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-4)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"ast-content-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4041","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-blog"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4041","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=4041"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4041\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4043,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4041\/revisions\/4043"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4041"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=4041"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=4041"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":4039,"date":"2026-07-07T17:02:49","date_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:32:49","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/?p=4039"},"modified":"2026-07-07T17:07:42","modified_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:37:42","slug":"episode-4-the-secret-life-of-a-spoonful-of-sugar","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/episode-4-the-secret-life-of-a-spoonful-of-sugar\/","title":{"rendered":"The Secret Life of a Spoonful of Sugar"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Have you ever wondered what happens after you stir sugar into your coffee?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Probably not.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Most of us are too busy looking for the biscuit.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">But imagine that tiny spoonful beginning a journey through your body.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It&#8217;s a bit like boarding an express train.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Some sugars hit the accelerator immediately.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They rush through the system, sending blood glucose climbing in record time.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Others prefer the scenic route.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Steadier.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">More measured.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Less dramatic.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The difference isn&#8217;t always visible in the sugar bowl.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It certainly isn&#8217;t written in giant letters on every packet.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Which is why scientists measure something called the Glycemic Index.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Think of it as a speedometer.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Not for cars.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For carbohydrates.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The lower the speed, the gentler the journey.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That&#8217;s why products like Sugarlif undergo independent Glycemic Index testing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Because when it comes to understanding how food behaves, assumptions are interesting.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Measurements are better.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So the next time you stir a spoonful into your tea, remember&#8230;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It may look ordinary.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">But every spoonful has a story.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Some simply have more science behind them than others.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Have you ever wondered what happens after you stir sugar into your coffee? Probably not. Most of us are too busy looking for the biscuit. But imagine that tiny spoonful beginning a journey through your body. It&#8217;s a bit like boarding an express train. Some sugars hit the accelerator immediately. They rush through the system, [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"site-sidebar-layout":"default","site-content-layout":"","ast-site-content-layout":"default","site-content-style":"default","site-sidebar-style":"default","ast-global-header-display":"","ast-banner-title-visibility":"","ast-main-header-display":"","ast-hfb-above-header-display":"","ast-hfb-below-header-display":"","ast-hfb-mobile-header-display":"","site-post-title":"","ast-breadcrumbs-content":"","ast-featured-img":"","footer-sml-layout":"","ast-disable-related-posts":"","theme-transparent-header-meta":"","adv-header-id-meta":"","stick-header-meta":"","header-above-stick-meta":"","header-main-stick-meta":"","header-below-stick-meta":"","astra-migrate-meta-layouts":"set","ast-page-background-enabled":"default","ast-page-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-4)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"ast-content-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4039","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-blog"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4039","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=4039"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4039\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4044,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4039\/revisions\/4044"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4039"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=4039"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=4039"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":4037,"date":"2026-07-07T17:02:10","date_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:32:10","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/?p=4037"},"modified":"2026-07-07T17:21:39","modified_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:51:39","slug":"episode-3-can-you-trust-a-food-label","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/episode-3-can-you-trust-a-food-label\/","title":{"rendered":"Can You Trust a Food Label?"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Let&#8217;s play a game.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Close your eyes.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">No, wait&#8230; keep reading.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Imagine you&#8217;re standing in front of a supermarket shelf.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One packet says <em>Natural.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Another says <em>Healthy.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A third proudly announces <em>Super Premium.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">By the time you&#8217;ve read five packets, you&#8217;ve apparently discovered foods that are natural, wholesome, authentic, artisanal, premium, handcrafted and probably blessed by unicorns.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s the uncomfortable truth.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A label can tell you almost anything.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Science cannot.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Science only tells you what&#8217;s true.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That&#8217;s why smart consumers have changed the question they ask.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They no longer ask&#8230;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>&#8220;What does the packet say?&#8221;<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They ask&#8230;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>&#8220;Who verified it?&#8221;<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Independent laboratories don&#8217;t have a favourite brand.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They don&#8217;t get impressed by glossy packaging.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They don&#8217;t care how many celebrities endorse a product.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They simply examine the evidence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It&#8217;s a wonderfully boring process.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Which is exactly how science should be.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Because your health deserves facts\u2014not adjectives.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The next time you&#8217;re shopping, admire the packaging if you like.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Then quietly ask yourself the only question that really matters.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>&#8220;Who checked the homework?&#8221;<\/em><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Let&#8217;s play a game. Close your eyes. No, wait&#8230; keep reading. Imagine you&#8217;re standing in front of a supermarket shelf. One packet says Natural. Another says Healthy. A third proudly announces Super Premium. By the time you&#8217;ve read five packets, you&#8217;ve apparently discovered foods that are natural, wholesome, authentic, artisanal, premium, handcrafted and probably blessed [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"site-sidebar-layout":"default","site-content-layout":"","ast-site-content-layout":"default","site-content-style":"default","site-sidebar-style":"default","ast-global-header-display":"","ast-banner-title-visibility":"","ast-main-header-display":"","ast-hfb-above-header-display":"","ast-hfb-below-header-display":"","ast-hfb-mobile-header-display":"","site-post-title":"","ast-breadcrumbs-content":"","ast-featured-img":"","footer-sml-layout":"","ast-disable-related-posts":"","theme-transparent-header-meta":"","adv-header-id-meta":"","stick-header-meta":"","header-above-stick-meta":"","header-main-stick-meta":"","header-below-stick-meta":"","astra-migrate-meta-layouts":"set","ast-page-background-enabled":"default","ast-page-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-4)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"ast-content-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4037","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-blog"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4037","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=4037"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4037\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4045,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4037\/revisions\/4045"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4037"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=4037"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=4037"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":4034,"date":"2026-07-07T17:00:57","date_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:30:57","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/?p=4034"},"modified":"2026-07-08T10:49:01","modified_gmt":"2026-07-08T05:19:01","slug":"episode-2-the-day-sugar-went-to-whistler","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/episode-2-the-day-sugar-went-to-whistler\/","title":{"rendered":"The Day Sugar Went to Whistler"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Every superhero has an origin story.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Batman had Gotham.<br>Superman had Krypton.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sugarlif?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It had&#8230; Whistler.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">No, not the snowy ski resort where people glide gracefully down mountains while the rest of us struggle to stay upright in borrowed boots.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We&#8217;re talking about the <strong>Whistler Carbohydrate Research Centre<\/strong>, where carbohydrates are studied with far more seriousness than most of us reserve for our annual health check-up.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now imagine being a humble spoonful of sugar.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One day you&#8217;re happily sweetening tea.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The next, you&#8217;re in a laboratory, being poked, prodded, measured and analysed by scientists who aren&#8217;t remotely interested in whether you make great gulab jamuns. They want answers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">How quickly are you digested?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">How does your glucose behave?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Do you really deserve to call yourself Low GI?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There are no participation trophies in science.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Nobody says, &#8220;Well done for trying.&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The numbers either support your claim\u2014or they don&#8217;t.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sugarlif went through that journey because extraordinary claims deserve extraordinary evidence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That&#8217;s the difference between saying <em>&#8220;Trust us.&#8221;<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And saying&#8230;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>&#8220;Here&#8217;s the science.&#8221;<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For consumers, that&#8217;s reassuring.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For scientists, that&#8217;s expected.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And for marketing departments&#8230;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Well, let&#8217;s just say science is a much tougher audience.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The next time someone tells you all sugars are exactly the same, remember that somewhere in the USA, there are laboratories whose entire job is proving that they&#8217;re not.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Turns out, even sugar sometimes has homework.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Every superhero has an origin story. Batman had Gotham.Superman had Krypton. Sugarlif? It had&#8230; Whistler. No, not the snowy ski resort where people glide gracefully down mountains while the rest of us struggle to stay upright in borrowed boots. We&#8217;re talking about the Whistler Carbohydrate Research Centre, where carbohydrates are studied with far more seriousness [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"site-sidebar-layout":"default","site-content-layout":"","ast-site-content-layout":"default","site-content-style":"default","site-sidebar-style":"default","ast-global-header-display":"","ast-banner-title-visibility":"","ast-main-header-display":"","ast-hfb-above-header-display":"","ast-hfb-below-header-display":"","ast-hfb-mobile-header-display":"","site-post-title":"","ast-breadcrumbs-content":"","ast-featured-img":"","footer-sml-layout":"","ast-disable-related-posts":"","theme-transparent-header-meta":"","adv-header-id-meta":"","stick-header-meta":"","header-above-stick-meta":"","header-main-stick-meta":"","header-below-stick-meta":"","astra-migrate-meta-layouts":"set","ast-page-background-enabled":"default","ast-page-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-4)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"ast-content-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-5)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""}},"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4034","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-blog"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4034","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=4034"}],"version-history":[{"count":3,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4034\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4052,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4034\/revisions\/4052"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4034"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=4034"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=4034"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":4032,"date":"2026-07-07T16:40:11","date_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:10:11","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/?p=4032"},"modified":"2026-07-07T16:40:11","modified_gmt":"2026-07-07T11:10:11","slug":"if-sugar-had-a-passport","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/natural-life.in\/if-sugar-had-a-passport\/","title":{"rendered":"If Sugar Had a Passport\u2026"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Imagine you&#8217;re standing in a supermarket, staring at two bags of sugar.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Both look almost identical.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Both are white.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Both promise sweetness.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Both are quietly judging your life choices.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So, how do you decide which one deserves a place in your kitchen?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You could trust the packaging. After all, every product seems to have a glowing story these days. &#8220;Natural.&#8221; &#8220;Healthy.&#8221; &#8220;Premium.&#8221; &#8220;Smart Choice.&#8221; If labels could talk any louder, they&#8217;d probably start singing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Or&#8230;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You could ask a far more important question.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>&#8220;Who tested it?&#8221;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Because when it comes to food, especially something as important as sugar, compliments from the manufacturer don&#8217;t count. That&#8217;s a bit like a student marking their own exam and proudly announcing, <em>&#8220;I got 100%!&#8221;<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Nice try.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is where Sugarlif takes a rather unusual journey.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Instead of simply telling the world it is a Low GI sugar, it packed its metaphorical bags and travelled all the way to <strong>GI Labs in Canada<\/strong>\u2014one of the world&#8217;s most respected laboratories dedicated to Glycemic Index testing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Think of GI Labs as the strict examiner nobody wants to bluff.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They&#8217;re not interested in fancy packaging.<br>They don&#8217;t care about clever advertising.<br>They certainly don&#8217;t hand out certificates because someone asked nicely.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A product either passes&#8230; or it doesn&#8217;t.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And Sugarlif did.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That&#8217;s important because a Low GI claim isn&#8217;t something consumers should accept on faith. It should be backed by independent scientific evaluation. That&#8217;s exactly what certification from GI Labs represents.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a world overflowing with marketing claims, independent validation is refreshingly boring.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And that&#8217;s actually a good thing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Science isn&#8217;t supposed to be dramatic. It&#8217;s supposed to be dependable.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For consumers, that means greater confidence that the product has been evaluated by experts whose only job is to measure what happens\u2014not what sounds good in a brochure.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Of course, none of this would matter if Sugarlif tasted like cardboard.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fortunately, it doesn&#8217;t.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It looks like sugar.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It tastes like sugar.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It sweetens your tea, coffee and desserts like sugar.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The difference isn&#8217;t in what your eyes see.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It&#8217;s in the science that quietly sits behind every spoonful.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So the next time someone tells you, &#8220;This product is healthy because the packet says so,&#8221; smile politely.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Then ask the question that really matters.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>&#8220;Who tested it?&#8221;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Because sometimes, the sweetest proof doesn&#8217;t come from advertising.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It comes from a laboratory halfway around the world.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Imagine you&#8217;re standing in a supermarket, staring at two bags of sugar. Both look almost identical. Both are white. Both promise sweetness. Both are quietly judging your life choices. So, how do you decide which one deserves a place in your kitchen? You could trust the packaging. After all, every product seems to have a [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"site-sidebar-layout":"default","site-content-layout":"","ast-site-content-layout":"default","site-content-style":"default","site-sidebar-style":"default","ast-global-header-display":"","ast-banner-title-visibility":"","ast-main-header-display":"","ast-hfb-above-header-display":"","ast-hfb-below-header-display":"","ast-hfb-mobile-header-display":"","site-post-title":"","ast-breadcrumbs-content":"","ast-featured-img":"","footer-sml-layout":"","ast-disable-related-posts":"","theme-transparent-header-meta":"","adv-header-id-meta":"","stick-header-meta":"","header-above-stick-meta":"","header-main-stick-meta":"","header-below-stick-meta":"","astra-migrate-meta-layouts":"set","ast-page-background-enabled":"default","ast-page-background-meta":{"desktop":{"background-color":"var(--ast-global-color-4)","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"tablet":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-type":"","background-media":"","overlay-type":"","overlay-color":"","overlay-opacity":"","overlay-gradient":""},"mobile":{"background-color":"","background-image":"","background-repeat":"repeat","background-position":"center center","background-size":"auto","background-attachment":"scroll","background-ty